1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
 - R.O. Porch, how we doing?

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:04,060
 We doing good this Tuesday night?

3
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,000
 Man, it's good to see ya.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,460
 If you didn't know, my name's Kylan,

5
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:09,380
 Executive Director of The Porch,

6
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:12,020
 and I have been gone for the last couple of weeks,

7
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:15,060
 and I am thrilled to be back.

8
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:18,620
 It's crazy, last night at like eight, nine p.m.,

9
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,300
 I was sitting there in the living room,

10
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,580
 and I just started to get this crazy headache,

11
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,620
 and I got these terrible body aches,

12
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,740
 and I just started getting those chills

13
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,780
 that just like shake you no matter how much you cover up,

14
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:33,900
 and I was like, oh my gosh, am I getting the flu?

15
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,100
 It's too soon, God, like I've got a flu appointment,

16
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,140
 a shot, this Thursday, like not yet, Lord,

17
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,100
 like let me get to the appointment first,

18
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,200
 and then I could just feel myself getting sick,

19
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,860
 and all night long, like I just tossed and I turned,

20
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:49,760
 and I was sick over the fact that I couldn't,

21
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,180
 I was sick over the fact, not that I was dealing

22
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:56,740
 with some sort of flu bug, or some sort of viral infection,

23
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:00,740
 but because I was just, I was sick of the thought

24
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:02,940
 of not being here with you.

25
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,820
 Like I've missed two weeks, and as I woke up this morning,

26
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:07,020
 and I knew, I was like, oh my gosh,

27
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:09,420
 like I don't know that I can get there, and I can do this,

28
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,380
 I nonetheless just decided to talk to the team,

29
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:14,620
 get them organized, and then seek the Lord,

30
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,780
 and God was like, you're not missing three weeks, buddy.

31
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:18,920
 Get back in on Tuesday night, and so here we are,

32
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,100
 I don't know if this is MJ's flu game or what,

33
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:23,100
 but I am going to give you everything I have

34
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,420
 over the course of our 40 minutes together or so.

35
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,380
 Does that sound good to you?

36
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:29,420
 Amazing, if you're wondering, why were you gone

37
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:30,700
 the last couple of weeks, I was gone

38
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:35,100
 because we had a baby girl, and she is officially here,

39
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,720
 not in the room, she will be in future weeks,

40
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:40,700
 but she is here in the world, and we have a photo of her,

41
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:45,100
 her name is Shiloh Lily Perry.

42
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,180
 Perry Party of Four has officially hit the scene,

43
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:52,100
 which we love, the reason why we named her Shiloh

44
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,040
 is because after Israel's wilderness wanderings,

45
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:57,300
 that was the first place, the very location

46
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,060
 where the presence of God in the tabernacle

47
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,420
 decided to reside.

48
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,700
 We want her to know by her first name

49
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,300
 that the presence of God is always with her.

50
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,560
 We named her Lily because we want her to consider

51
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,860
 those flowers of the field so she will know

52
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,540
 where her value is found.

53
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,300
 It's not found in what the world says,

54
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,620
 it's not found in what some doofus guy has to say,

55
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:20,900
 it's not found in whatever she's able to achieve in life,

56
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,900
 it is found in what God has said is true of her.

57
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:27,140
 And I'm thrilled to introduce you to the Porch family.

58
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,920
 So thanks for praying for us, if you've been praying for us,

59
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,900
 she is genuinely a bundle of joy,

60
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:36,180
 we could not feel as if we are under more of God's

61
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:40,420
 undeserved kindness in this season, he is so good to us.

62
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:41,820
 You don't get to pick how these things go,

63
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,260
 we could not have picked better.

64
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,940
 And so glory to God, it's been amazing,

65
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,660
 so glad that she's here, and so glad that I'm here,

66
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:50,660
 and that we get the chance to dive in together.

67
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:52,220
 I'll start by just saying this,

68
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:54,620
 when we were at the hospital with Shiloh,

69
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:59,380
 I couldn't help but be reminded of the deja vu effect

70
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:00,800
 of what that experience was like

71
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:03,180
 when we had our first go around with our firstborn

72
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,780
 just a couple of years ago.

73
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:06,700
 And what we knew about that experience

74
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:09,400
 was everyone had told us how amazing that first day

75
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,420
 was gonna be as a family, which they were right,

76
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,940
 like your first day as a family is incredible,

77
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:17,900
 but what we were not told is how awful that first night

78
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,180
 was going to be as a family.

79
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,980
 Not because you're up every couple of hours

80
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:23,740
 having to feed the baby, we expected that much.

81
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:25,220
 We knew that that was gonna be the case.

82
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,800
 That was not the thing that caught us off guard.

83
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,500
 What caught us off guard was the fact

84
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,760
 that this kid just spontaneously choked on his own spit

85
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,620
 over and over and over and over the course of the night.

86
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:37,060
 I'd heard people joke about trying to keep their kids alive,

87
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,380
 but this was no laughing matter.

88
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,180
 We were literally in the throes of trying to help

89
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:44,420
 a little newborn baby, 24 hours, 48 hours old,

90
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:48,900
 breathe so that way he could move on to the next day.

91
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:49,940
 I knew things were gonna get dicey

92
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,100
 when we got back into the real world.

93
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,620
 I was not expecting them to get dicey

94
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:54,580
 while we were at the hospital.

95
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,740
 And what's crazy about it is as we're laying there a night,

96
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:01,180
 listening so that way we can hear if he does choke,

97
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,820
 equipped with nothing but just like one of those,

98
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:05,300
 like a squishy little snot syringes.

99
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,260
 You know what I'm talking about?

100
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:08,020
 You will if you don't.

101
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,180
 I kept thinking to myself,

102
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:12,580
 this is so much harder than I ever expected.

103
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,780
 And as we went through the first hour of the night

104
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,140
 into the second hour of the night,

105
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:17,340
 into the third hour of the night,

106
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,980
 and then we crept into the fourth hour of the night,

107
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:22,780
 and I just could feel the fatigue setting in,

108
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,940
 our nurse finally walked in in the fifth,

109
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:25,980
 and she looked at us and she goes,

110
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,260
 "Hey, would y'all like me to take the baby

111
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,700
 "so you guys can get some rest?"

112
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,740
 What?

113
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:31,420
 That's an option?

114
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,580
 You'll take the baby so we can sleep?

115
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:35,100
 Yes, check please.

116
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,420
 You can take her right now.

117
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:37,580
 You can have him now.

118
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:40,060
 We will take some sleep if you're willing to take him

119
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,420
 for the next extended hours.

120
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,340
 And so she took that baby,

121
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,820
 and what we realized is that the presence

122
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:48,380
 of that blessed one, all our needs were met instantly.

123
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:52,820
 We didn't have to do parenting in that moment

124
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:53,740
 on our own strength anymore.

125
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,620
 We could rely on the strength of someone

126
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:58,380
 that actually was more experienced than we were.

127
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,820
 Now, why do I tell you all of that?

128
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,140
 Because we are looking at a passage of scripture today

129
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,780
 where one man is caught in a moment

130
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:07,780
 that is so similar to that experience for me.

131
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:12,320
 It is a moment that is somehow so awesome, incredible.

132
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:16,660
 It's unbelievable, and yet it is simultaneously

133
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,460
 somehow still awful.

134
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:22,180
 What do I mean by that?

135
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:28,180
 He encountered the presence of the blessed one,

136
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:29,500
 and at the presence of the blessed one,

137
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,660
 he realized that one, God,

138
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:38,720
 is terrifying because of his awesomeness,

139
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:42,300
 and yet he is wonderful because of his compassion.

140
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:46,140
 He has invited me in, and so what I want to do tonight

141
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,820
 is I just want to look at that text of scripture with you,

142
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:51,460
 this place in the Bible where we see someone

143
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:55,640
 come face-to-face with God, enthroned above it all,

144
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:59,700
 and the place that we find it is in the book of Isaiah.

145
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,180
 So if you have a Bible, turn with me to Isaiah.

146
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:04,460
 While you're doing that, you're probably wondering,

147
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:07,160
 is this the next part in our series Lovers?

148
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,100
 It's not.

149
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,260
 This is not the next part.

150
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:11,180
 We're gonna be back in Lovers next week,

151
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:12,700
 and I am so eager, geeked out,

152
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,580
 to get back into that text with you,

153
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,260
 but I just wanted to spend tonight

154
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,780
 sharing with you some things that have just been

155
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:20,540
 on my heart over the course of the last couple of weeks

156
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:22,620
 as I've been meeting with God, sitting on my back porch,

157
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:25,340
 and praying about you all, because here's the thing

158
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:28,980
 that I am desperately passionate about here at the porch.

159
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:33,680
 I want this place to be a place of answered prayer,

160
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,700
 not just a place of prayer.

161
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,300
 I want God to answer our prayers here.

162
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:39,540
 I want him to show up, listen in,

163
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:42,260
 and deliver on the things that you're asking for,

164
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:43,740
 not because you're deserving,

165
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,940
 but because it will glorify him if he would so do it,

166
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,300
 and yet as I was talking to him about like,

167
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,740
 God, please, let this be a place where you answer prayer.

168
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,640
 When you do, God, things change for people.

169
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:56,180
 They begin to realize you are who you say you are.

170
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:59,820
 I felt the subtle whisper of the Spirit.

171
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:04,220
 Say, Kylan, I want to do what my people are asking,

172
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:07,460
 but are they wanting to do what I'm asking?

173
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:10,400
 I am willing to answer them,

174
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,100
 but are they willing to answer me?

175
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:15,300
 I was struck by that.

176
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:20,460
 Because it's not enough for the porch to be a place

177
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:21,420
 where we meet new friends.

178
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:22,860
 That's a good thing.

179
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,340
 It's not enough for the porch to be a place

180
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,420
 where we learn the Scriptures.

181
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,180
 That's a great thing.

182
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:29,940
 It's not enough for the porch to be a place

183
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:33,340
 where we gather and worship God on high.

184
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:36,040
 That's incredible too.

185
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:41,100
 No, it is only enough that when through the means

186
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:45,380
 of this all, we actually are changed as a result.

187
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:47,920
 We are actually transformed on the other side.

188
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,400
 That the person you walked in as,

189
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,380
 what if this were true for you tonight?

190
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:53,300
 That the person you walked in here as,

191
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:56,140
 whatever it is you're excited about in your story,

192
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,440
 whatever it is you're disappointed about

193
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,400
 when you look yourself in the face,

194
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:02,180
 what if that could actually be different

195
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:04,340
 by the time you walked out?

196
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:06,860
 What if you could leave better?

197
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:10,620
 Not just more moral, but more like Christ?

198
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:11,700
 That's what he wants to do.

199
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,740
 He wants to transform.

200
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,020
 He wants to change.

201
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,740
 The question is though,

202
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:19,180
 are we willing to appropriately respond to him?

203
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:23,580
 That when he calls, when he asks, when he commends,

204
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:25,580
 we would say yes.

205
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,300
 Yes, God, I'm here, I'm in.

206
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,700
 What do you want me to do?

207
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,620
 I will respond appropriately.

208
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,020
 The truth of the matter is,

209
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,660
 that's what Isaiah is getting at.

210
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,740
 This is a man that sees God, sees himself,

211
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,620
 and then responds accordingly.

212
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:43,100
 And I'm praying that would happen for you, porch family.

213
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,080
 So here's what it says.

214
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,620
 It says this in Isaiah 6, one through three,

215
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:49,620
 knowing the reality is we're all gonna respond

216
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:50,460
 to something in life,

217
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:53,300
 but there's only one that's worthy of responding to in life.

218
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,740
 It says this in verse one.

219
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:59,620
 In the year that King Uzziah died,

220
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:02,220
 I saw the Lord sitting upon a throne.

221
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,100
 He was high and lifted up,

222
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,980
 and the train of his robe filled the temple.

223
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:08,100
 Above him stood the seraphim.

224
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,700
 Each had six wings, with two he covered his face,

225
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,940
 with two he covered his feet,

226
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,340
 and with two he flew.

227
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:14,800
 And one called to another and said,

228
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:18,380
 "Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts.

229
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,900
 "The whole earth is full of his glory."

230
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:25,960
 These seraphim, what the Hebrew describes

231
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,220
 as these burning ones,

232
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,060
 because that's what happens

233
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:30,260
 when you're in the presence of God, you burn.

234
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:35,260
 They make a massive claim about God.

235
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:41,380
 They say that he is holy, holy, holy.

236
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:45,180
 And that claim changes everything for Isaiah in this moment

237
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:49,020
 because God's holiness puts everything in perspective.

238
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,460
 God's holiness puts everything in perspective.

239
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:53,660
 It says that in the year King Uzziah died,

240
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:56,660
 I saw the Lord sitting upon a throne.

241
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:58,460
 Now, typically, we read this

242
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,180
 and we just race by this little detail

243
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:02,500
 because we're not real sure who King Uzziah is

244
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,960
 or why that would be significant to us.

245
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,220
 But what we need to realize

246
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:08,500
 is that King Uzziah was the greatest king in Judah

247
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,740
 since the time of King Solomon.

248
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:13,180
 He reigned for 52 years

249
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:16,540
 and he expanded the borders of Israel

250
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:17,980
 in ways that other kings could not.

251
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,300
 They were greater in power,

252
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:20,580
 they were greater in provision,

253
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,620
 and they were greater in militant might.

254
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,620
 Like they were a better nation under King Uzziah

255
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:28,420
 until his pride got the best of him and he died.

256
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:31,420
 And it's in that moment,

257
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,580
 after everyone has been sleeping soundly at night

258
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:35,540
 because King Uzziah is on the throne,

259
