00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:53,300
 It says that the foundations of the threshold shook,

525
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:58,420
 meaning an inanimate object,

526
00:21:58,420 --> 00:22:04,060
 a lifeless room couldn't help but be moved

527
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:07,300
 at the fact that God was holy, holy, holy,

528
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:09,100
 and yet you wanna know what's crazy.

529
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:11,580
 So many of us with breath in our lungs,

530
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,100
 hearts beating in our chests,

531
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:15,020
 emotions streaming from our eyes,

532
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:17,980
 we are not moving near like the room.

533
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:19,660
 Like we're not shaking, we're not stirred,

534
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:20,940
 we're not moved, why?

535
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:24,820
 Because our worship is not about him, it's about us.

536
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:26,540
 We walk in and we worry about

537
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:27,740
 what people are gonna think of us.

538
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:30,300
 And here's the thing, I've had all of the conversations.

539
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:31,140
 Kylan, listen, man,

540
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:32,740
 it's just not my personality to put my hands up.

541
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:34,340
 It's just not my personality to hit my knees.

542
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:35,220
 It's just not my personality.

543
00:22:35,220 --> 00:22:37,060
 Listen, this is not about your personality.

544
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:38,940
 This is about the presence of God.

545
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,540
 That's what this is about.

546
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:42,620
 There's only one right response,

547
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:45,780
 and the right response is to worship him,

548
00:22:45,780 --> 00:22:49,780
 to be moved as the threshold is moved.

549
00:22:49,780 --> 00:22:51,580
 His presence demands a response.

550
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:54,180
 Luke 19, 37 through 40, I love this.

551
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:56,140
 This is the ultimate mic drop by Jesus.

552
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:58,940
 He says this, as he was drawing near,

553
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:00,620
 already on the way down the Mount of Olives,

554
00:23:00,620 --> 00:23:02,860
 the whole multitude of his disciples began to rejoice

555
00:23:02,860 --> 00:23:03,920
 and praise God with a loud voice

556
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:06,140
 for all the mighty works that they had seen.

557
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:07,740
 They were saying, "Blessed is the king

558
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:09,060
 "who comes in the name of the Lord.

559
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:10,940
 "Peace in heaven, glory in the highest."

560
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:12,540
 And some of the Pharisees,

561
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:15,340
 those that were in the crowd, they said to him,

562
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:17,900
 "Teacher, rebuke your disciples."

563
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:23,180
 I would have loved to have seen the look on their faces

564
00:23:23,180 --> 00:23:26,460
 when he told them, even if these were silent,

565
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:29,220
 their stones would cry out.

566
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:32,900
 You ever thought about that in here?

567
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:36,100
 And when you walk in, whether you want to or not,

568
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:38,060
 the room's about to rock.

569
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:39,360
 Why?

570
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:42,340
 Because God's worthy of rocking and moving

571
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:44,740
 and stirring and shaking you for.

572
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:46,460
 That's the kind of response he deserves.

573
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:48,140
 That's what happens in this space.

574
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:49,820
 Not because of what we do, how good we are,

575
00:23:49,820 --> 00:23:51,740
 how gifted or talented we can seem,

576
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:54,780
 but because of how good he is, how great he is.

577
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:56,080
 That's the right response.

578
00:23:56,080 --> 00:24:02,540
 God's gonna get his.

579
00:24:02,540 --> 00:24:05,500
 And here's the thing.

580
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:07,140
 God doesn't need you to worship him,

581
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:08,180
 doesn't need you to praise him,

582
00:24:08,180 --> 00:24:10,740
 doesn't need you to respond to him because he's insecure.

583
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:14,300
 He wants you to respond to him because he knows we are.

584
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:15,140
 He wants you to respond to him

585
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:17,420
 because he knows we're the ones that are secure.

586
00:24:17,420 --> 00:24:18,460
 Like the girl you're trying to impress,

587
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:20,980
 she isn't gonna make you feel more secure than God can.

588
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:22,300
 That corner office or that pay bump

589
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:23,460
 that you're desperate to get,

590
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:25,700
 it's not gonna make you feel more secure than God can.

591
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:26,860
 Fame and influence,

592
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:28,540
 it's not gonna make you feel more secure than God can.

593
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:30,780
 Having that body, thinner, stronger, whatever,

594
00:24:30,780 --> 00:24:32,860
 it's not gonna make you more secure than God can.

595
00:24:32,860 --> 00:24:34,860
 Why does God want us to worship him?

596
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:36,980
 Because when we worship him, here's the truth,

597
00:24:36,980 --> 00:24:39,660
 we stop worshiping ourselves.

598
00:24:39,660 --> 00:24:41,540
 And we get back in step with the rest of creation

599
00:24:41,540 --> 00:24:44,860
 and we worship he who alone is worthy of it.

600
00:24:44,860 --> 00:24:47,020
 And he does it for a good.

601
00:24:47,020 --> 00:24:50,180
 The seraphim, it says they hide their face and their feet.

602
00:24:50,180 --> 00:24:53,540
 The threshold shakes at the sound of his name.

603
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:55,420
 And Isaiah freaks out.

604
00:24:55,420 --> 00:24:57,820
 He says, I am lost.

605
00:24:57,820 --> 00:25:02,360
 The Hebrew, it's better translated as I am silent,

606
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,900
 which is saying something.

607
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:05,780
 Because what's Isaiah's occupation?

608
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:10,660
 He's a prophet, which means his voice,

609
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:12,500
 it's kind of his moneymaker.

610
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:13,820
 It's kind of his calling card.

611
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:15,060
 It's sort of the thing that he's known for.

612
00:25:15,060 --> 00:25:16,380
 It's his greatest strength.

613
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:18,460
 It's the essence of his reputation.

614
00:25:18,460 --> 00:25:19,480
 It's what when he walks in the room,

615
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:21,060
 everyone is able to identify him by.

616
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:23,580
 He says, the very thing that is strongest in me

617
00:25:23,580 --> 00:25:25,700
 is weakest in the face of God.

618
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:29,140
 I am silent.

619
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:34,900
 I am silent.

620
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:39,660
 And the reason he is,

621
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:44,640
 is not that he didn't have the words to speak.

622
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:49,080
 It's that he didn't have the worth to speak them.

623
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:53,940
 It's not that he didn't have the words to speak.

624
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:55,940
 He didn't have the worth to speak them.

625
00:25:55,940 --> 00:25:57,980
 At the sight of God, in all his holiness,

626
00:25:57,980 --> 00:26:02,220
 in all his splendor, even Isaiah's best strength falls short.

627
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:04,540
 His lips are unclean, his words are too short,

628
00:26:04,540 --> 00:26:07,140
 his voice falls silent.

629
00:26:07,140 --> 00:26:09,820
 You ever been in a moment like that?

630
00:26:09,820 --> 00:26:11,200
 With the presence of someone's greatness,

631
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:13,080
 you sense your smallness?

632
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:18,000
 It happened to me a little over a year ago.

633
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,880
 I was gathered with a group of young adult pastors,

634
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,060
 pastors from around the country,

635
00:26:22,060 --> 00:26:23,940
 and we got the privilege of listening

636
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:27,580
 to a 190-year-old Chuck Swindoll.

637
00:26:27,580 --> 00:26:30,300
 And if you don't know who Chuck is, Chuck is the man.

638
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:33,660
 Like, he is one of the greatest pastors

639
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:36,620
 and preachers of the 21st century,

640
00:26:36,620 --> 00:26:41,620
 as well as the history of Christianity.

641
00:26:41,620 --> 00:26:46,120
 And the reason it was so incredible to sit with him

642
00:26:46,120 --> 00:26:48,060
 was not because we got to have conversation,

643
00:26:48,060 --> 00:26:49,500
 but because we just got to listen.

644
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:53,780
 Not a single guy in that room dared speak over Chuck,

645
00:26:53,780 --> 00:26:56,500
 because he was supremely greater

646
00:26:56,500 --> 00:26:59,740
 at everything we were aspiring to be great in.

647
00:27:00,820 --> 00:27:03,100
 The room was filled with teachers and leaders

648
00:27:03,100 --> 00:27:03,940
 and counselors.

649
00:27:03,940 --> 00:27:07,020
 Like, some of them, they preached to huge rooms,

650
00:27:07,020 --> 00:27:10,620
 and yet none of us have our sermons broadcast

651
00:27:10,620 --> 00:27:12,060
 across 1,000 different radio stations

652
00:27:12,060 --> 00:27:14,780
 in multiple languages all across the world.

653
00:27:14,780 --> 00:27:19,180
 Like, some of us, we have preached powerfully,

654
00:27:19,180 --> 00:27:20,740
 and yet we're not heralded

655
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:23,740
 as one of the two most influential pastors

656
00:27:23,740 --> 00:27:25,300
 next to Billy Graham himself.

657
00:27:25,300 --> 00:27:29,620
 Like, we are not in any way as great as Chuck.

658
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:31,180
 In fact, in the presence of his greatness,

659
00:27:31,180 --> 00:27:32,900
 we recognized our smallness.

660
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:34,380
 That's what should happen to us

661
00:27:34,380 --> 00:27:35,860
 in the presence of a holy God.

662
00:27:35,860 --> 00:27:37,340
 That's why when we come in this room

663
00:27:37,340 --> 00:27:39,780
 and we gather to worship, we gather to learn,

664
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:42,420
 we gather to pray, we should know

665
00:27:42,420 --> 00:27:43,740
 that there should be something stirring,

666
00:27:43,740 --> 00:27:45,700
 changing inside of us.

667
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:49,600
 Because God is here, and that changes the atmosphere.

668
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:51,220
 That's what happens in the presence of a holy God.

669
00:27:51,220 --> 00:27:52,380
 So whatever your thing is,

670
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:53,540
 whatever you find your strength in,

671
00:27:53,540 --> 00:27:56,180
 you build your reputation on, you pride yourself in,

672
00:27:56,180 --> 00:27:59,680
 all of that is forgettable in the face of a holy God.

673
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:02,980
 We don't pride ourselves on what we've achieved.

674
00:28:02,980 --> 00:28:06,260
 We pity ourselves because it's not enough.

675
00:28:06,260 --> 00:28:09,460
 Which can feel like really bad news

676
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:10,820
 until you read verse six.

677
00:28:10,820 --> 00:28:11,700
 Look at verse six.

678
00:28:11,700 --> 00:28:15,780
 Then one of the seraphim flew to me,

679
00:28:15,780 --> 00:28:17,120
 having in his hand a burning coal

680
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,820
 that he'd taken with tongs from the altar.

681
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:19,660
 He touched my mouth and he said,

682
00:28:19,660 --> 00:28:22,340
 "Hey, behold, this has touched your lips.

683
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:25,100
 "Your guilt is taken away, and your sin is atoned for."

684
00:28:26,940 --> 00:28:27,860
 It's interesting.

685
00:28:27,860 --> 00:28:35,620
 Woe is me, man of unclean lips, people of unclean lips.

686
00:28:35,620 --> 00:28:39,860
 Isaiah understands just how dire his situation is.

687
00:28:39,860 --> 00:28:42,820
 He understands just how desperate his needs are,

688
00:28:42,820 --> 00:28:45,500
 and yet he never tries to get right with God.

689
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:46,380
 He never does it.

690
00:28:46,380 --> 00:28:49,180
 He never begs God for mercy, he never offers a sacrifice,

691
00:28:49,180 --> 00:28:53,380
 he never seeks forgiveness, which is completely implausible.

692
00:28:53,380 --> 00:28:56,020
 Like it is the natural instinct of every person in this room

693
00:28:56,020 --> 00:28:58,860
 when they do something wrong to try to make up for it, yeah?

694
00:28:58,860 --> 00:29:00,260
 So like on the rare occasion

695
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:03,220
 that I do something wrong to my wife,

696
00:29:03,220 --> 00:29:07,140
 I find myself doing God knows what to try and make amends.

697
00:29:07,140 --> 00:29:09,260
 I'm like cleaning gutters, and buying flowers,

698
00:29:09,260 --> 00:29:11,340
 and scrubbing dishes, and hanging ceiling fans,

699
00:29:11,340 --> 00:29:13,460
 and doing all manner of different things

700
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:16,700
 just 'cause I want to get back in her good graces.

701
00:29:16,700 --> 00:29:18,180
 But Isaiah doesn't do that.

702
00:29:18,180 --> 00:29:21,260
 Like he doesn't roll out the 10-step path

703
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:23,380
 to getting in God's favor.

704
00:29:23,380 --> 00:29:26,380
 He doesn't perform some grand gesture

705
00:29:26,380 --> 00:29:29,460
 that gets him back into God's good grace.

706
00:29:29,460 --> 00:29:30,620
 He doesn't do any of it.

707
00:29:30,620 --> 00:29:34,540
 All he does is he just gets contrite over his sin.

708
00:29:34,540 --> 00:29:37,460
 And the amazing thing is that's enough,

709
00:29:37,460 --> 00:29:40,400
 because we're saved by God's offering, not our own.

710
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:43,060
 It's not what you do, it's what he does.

711
00:29:43,060 --> 00:29:45,620
 Notice in what way Isaiah's sin is atoned for.

712
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:48,120
 It's atoned through a burning coal from the altar.

713
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:51,860
 Growing up, I would camp with my family,

714
00:29:52,860 --> 00:29:56,380
 and at the end of the day, as the sun would set,

715
00:29:56,380 --> 00:29:58,780
 and the day would draw to an end,

716
00:29:58,780 --> 00:30:01,020
 we would often do what many of you, I'm sure, have.

717
00:30:01,020 --> 00:30:03,100
 We would build a fire.

718
00:30:03,100 --> 00:30:05,460
 And what you know, if you've built fires before,

719
00:30:05,460 --> 00:30:09,580
 is you know that coals, they are the byproduct

720
00:30:09,580 --> 00:30:12,240
 of not a fire that's been assembled,

721
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:14,460
 but a fire that's been burned.

722
00:30:14,460 --> 00:30:16,460
 Once the kindling has been gathered,

723
00:30:16,460 --> 00:30:21,460
 the flames have risen, and everything is burnt up.

724
00:30:21,580 --> 00:30:26,500
 The result is a glowing coal at the bottom of its bed,

725
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:32,860
 in the same way that coals are indicative

726
00:30:32,860 --> 00:30:34,760
 of a fire that's been burned.

727
00:30:34,760 --> 00:30:37,740
 Coals from an altar are indicative

728
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:40,460
 of a sacrifice that's been made.

729
00:30:40,460 --> 00:30:44,620
 Who made the sacrifice?

730
00:30:44,620 --> 00:30:47,740
 Wasn't Isaiah.

731
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:49,540
 All he does is bring his contrition.

732
00:30:50,780 --> 00:30:55,060
 And yet God, through Christ, brings the necessary perfection.

733
00:30:55,060 --> 00:31:00,060
 He offers the one who can atone for Isaiah's and mine,

734
00:31:00,060 --> 00:31:03,660
 and your sins completely.

735
00:31:03,660 --> 00:31:04,760
 He offers Christ.

736
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:09,780
 Isaiah 57, 15 says,

737
00:31:09,780 --> 00:31:12,780
 for this is what the high and the exalted one says,

738
00:31:12,780 --> 00:31:15,700
 he who lives forever, whose name is holy.

739
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:18,740
 I live in a high, and I live in a holy place,

740
00:31:18,740 --> 00:31:23,060
 but also with the one who is contrite,

741
00:31:23,060 --> 00:31:26,940
 and lowly in spirit, to revive the spirit of the lowly,

742
00:31:26,940 --> 00:31:29,180
 and to revive the heart of the contrite.

743
00:31:29,180 --> 00:31:31,300
 You see, friends, God is not looking for perfection

744
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:33,980
 in his people, he is looking for contrition.

745
00:31:33,980 --> 00:31:36,140
 But you know who's looking for perfection?

746
00:31:36,140 --> 00:31:37,540
 We are.

747
00:31:37,540 --> 00:31:39,900
 That's why so many of us,

748
00:31:39,900 --> 00:31:43,100
 we unconsciously try to atone for our sins.

749
00:31:43,100 --> 00:31:47,580
 It's why before we confess that we looked at porn,

750
00:31:47,580 --> 00:31:49,880
 we try to go two weeks without looking at porn,

751
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:51,300
 because we wanna be able to approach someone

752
00:31:51,300 --> 00:31:54,580
 and feel a little bit more perfect in their eyes

753
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:57,740
 than we were had we come from the very beginning.

754
00:31:57,740 --> 00:31:59,940
 It's why some of you, you're working so hard

755
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:01,460
 to heap up knowledge and to learn,

756
00:32:01,460 --> 00:32:03,260
 not because you're just fascinated by the scriptures

757
00:32:03,260 --> 00:32:04,660
 and you're trying to build your ego on it,

758
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:07,600
 no, because you're desperate to know who God is

759
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:09,180
 and make yourself right before him,

760
00:32:09,180 --> 00:32:10,740
 when in reality, you cannot.

761
00:32:10,740 --> 00:32:13,180
 We are unconsciously trying to atone for our sins,

762
00:32:13,180 --> 00:32:14,120
 and God is looking at you and saying,

763
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:17,780
 stop, stop doing that, you cannot atone for your sins,

764
00:32:17,780 --> 00:32:20,460
 nor should you, I have atoned for them.

765
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:23,260
 All you have to do is bring me contrition,

766
00:32:23,260 --> 00:32:27,220
 contrition, conviction, not emotion.

767
00:32:27,220 --> 00:32:32,140
 Come to me with contrition, be honest about where you're at,

768
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:34,500
 and I'll be honest about where we're going,

769
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:36,300
 and God will move you forward,

770
00:32:36,300 --> 00:32:38,640
 not in the ways you wanna go, but in the ways he wants to go

771
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:42,220
 and that is for your good, that is for your good.

772
00:32:42,220 --> 00:32:44,100
 You cannot save yourself, God knows it,

773
00:32:44,100 --> 00:32:46,180
 he knows every one of us is totally incapable

774
00:32:46,180 --> 00:32:48,780
 of satisfying his holy wrath against sin.

775
00:32:48,780 --> 00:32:50,660
 He knows there's no service, there's no sacrament,

776
00:32:50,660 --> 00:32:53,320
 there's no sacrifice that we can ever offer

777
00:32:53,320 --> 00:32:56,260
 to make up for our sin against his holy name,

778
00:32:56,260 --> 00:32:58,240
 but he also knows that there is nonetheless

779
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,180
 still a way for you to be saved.

780
00:33:00,180 --> 00:33:03,260
 For though you cannot save yourselves before a holy God,

781
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:04,660
 that holy God has saved you.

